WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.537
What holds up your workbench can also hold your tools.

00:00:05.817 --> 00:00:07.112
Legs or cabinets?

00:00:07.392 --> 00:00:10.089
It is one of the most useful choices you will make.

00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:14.543
Open space under a bench often ends up as a dumping ground.

00:00:14.823 --> 00:00:19.134
Boxes pile up, tools disappear, and operators lose their legroom.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:24.495
A leg frame keeps the area open for legroom, a footrest or a bottom shelf.

00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:26.693
A base cabinet replaces the leg,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:31.248
carrying the worktop while giving you lockable drawers right where you work.

00:00:31.528 --> 00:00:36.213
You can mix both: one leg frame and one cabinet is a very popular layout.

00:00:36.493 --> 00:00:41.057
Cabinets also add weight low down, which makes the whole bench feel more solid.

00:00:41.657 --> 00:00:44.507
On Furnisys Scitec and Pro benches,

00:00:44.507 --> 00:00:50.858
base cabinets of 16.85 or 22.20 inches wide can take the place of a leg frame,

00:00:50.858 --> 00:00:54.197
so storage becomes part of the structure.

00:00:54.797 --> 00:00:58.307
So decide by what the operator needs below the worktop.

00:00:58.587 --> 00:01:00.070
What would you store under your bench?

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:05.133
Comment below, and next, find out why long benches need a top support rail.

00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:09.978
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

